# React

Builds on `code-javascript`. Prefer the project's React major and existing
router/state/data libraries — do not introduce a second stack unless asked.

## Components

- Function components only; no new class components
- One component, one job; extract subcomponents when JSX or handlers sprawl
- Props are a public contract — type them (TypeScript or PropTypes/JSDoc) and
  keep required vs optional honest
- Prefer composition and children over deep prop drilling; use context only for
  truly cross-cutting values (theme, auth session), not for every shared value
- Keep render pure: no network, random, or store writes during render

## Hooks

- Follow the Rules of Hooks (top level only; no conditional/looped hooks)
- `useEffect` for syncing with external systems — not for deriving state that
  can be computed during render
- List effect dependencies correctly; do not disable `exhaustive-deps` to hide
  bugs. Prefer restructuring over broad omission
- Cleanup subscriptions, timers, and abort controllers in effect cleanups
- Prefer local state; lift state only when multiple siblings need it
- When the project uses React Compiler (or equivalent), do not add
  `useMemo` / `useCallback` by default — only when profiling or an existing
  pattern requires it
- Prefer modern primitives the project already uses (`useEffectEvent`,
  `startTransition`, `useDeferredValue`) over ad-hoc ref hacks when they fit

## Events and async

- Handlers: name for the user action (`onSubmit`, `handleSave`); keep them thin
- Abort in-flight fetches on unmount or dependency change when results would
  call `setState`
- Do not ignore promise rejections; surface errors to UI or the project's
  error boundary pattern

## Lists and keys

- Stable keys from identity (`id`), never array index for reorderable lists,
  never `Math.random()`
- Extract list item components when the row has non-trivial UI or hooks

## Safety and a11y

- Follow `code-security` for XSS: no unsanitized `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`
- Prefer semantic HTML and labeled controls; do not replace buttons/links with
  clickable `div`s
- Preserve focus management for dialogs and menus the project already uses

## Tests

- Prefer Testing Library-style tests (user-visible behavior) over implementation
  details when the repo has that runner
- Ship lasting component/hook tests in the same change as new **core** UI
  behavior when a UI test runner exists (`code-unit-testing`)
